## 5. Technical Requirements

### 5.1 Mobile app

- Platforms: Android 8.0 (API 26) and above, iOS 15 and above. Design for low-end Android (2 GB RAM) first.
- Size and speed: installed size under 25 MB and cold start under 3 seconds on a mid-range device.
- Background location: Android Geofencing API with ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION; iOS region monitoring with Always authorisation. Neither runs a continuous foreground service, which protects battery.
- Manufacturer battery managers: Tecno, Infinix, itel, Xiaomi and some Samsung models aggressively kill background apps. Ship an in-app setup guide per manufacturer and detect when geofences stop firing.
- Bluetooth: scan for the entrance beacon only inside the service window to save battery.
- Push: FCM high-priority data messages; APNs with time-sensitive priority for arrival confirmations.
- Local storage: encrypted SQLite for the offline queue and cached profile.
- Accessibility: WCAG 2.2 AA, dynamic text sizing, screen reader labels.
- Languages: English at launch; string files ready for Twi, Ga, Ewe and French.
- Store compliance: Google Play requires a background location declaration with a demo video, and Apple requires clear purpose strings. Plan for review time.

### 5.2 Backend and platform

| Area | Requirement |
|---|---|
| Availability | 99.9% monthly. Treat Sunday 07:00 to 14:00 as peak: no deployments from Saturday 18:00 to Sunday 18:00 |
| Peak load | Pilot: 2,000 members, about 1,500 arrival signals in 30 minutes with bursts near 20 per second. Design for 20 times that |
| Latency | p95 under 400 ms for check-in endpoints; dashboards under 1.5 s |
| Data growth | About 100,000 attendance rows per church per year; partition attendance tables by year |
| Recovery | RPO 15 minutes, RTO 2 hours |
| Scaling | Stateless API behind a load balancer; add a read replica when needed |
| Idempotency | Required on signals, check-ins and payments |
| Phone numbers | Normalise to E.164 (Ghana: 024 123 4567 becomes +233241234567); unique per tenant |
| Time | Store UTC, display in the tenant time zone (Africa/Accra by default) |
| Email | SPF, DKIM and DMARC on the sending domain; handle bounces and complaints |
| SMS | Registered sender ID, delivery-receipt webhooks, per-tenant spending caps |
| Browsers | Last two versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari; admin web responsive down to tablet |
| Imports | CSV import with duplicate detection on phone and name, with a preview before commit |

### 5.3 Quality and testing

- Unit tests on core rules (attendance resolver, absence detection, permissions), end-to-end tests on every check-in path.
- Real-device lab: Tecno, Infinix, itel, Samsung A-series, one low-end iPhone and one recent iPhone.
- Field tests at the actual church premises, walking and driving, indoors and outdoors, before choosing radii.
- Load test at 20 times the pilot peak before launch.
- Monitoring and alerting on check-in success rate, queue depth, push and SMS delivery rates and geofence-silence anomalies.

