### 6.7 Edge cases

| Situation | Behaviour |
|---|---|
| Member drives past without stopping | Dwell rule prevents a check-in |
| GPS drift places someone inside the ring from a nearby building | Geofence alone gives medium confidence; the dwell rule and a beacon or usher scan raise it |
| Phone off or battery saver on | Email or SMS link before service, or usher check-in |
| Arrives late | Accepted until the window closes; marked late after the start time |
| Leaves early | Departure recorded if enabled; attendance still counts |
| Shared household phone | The app supports multiple household profiles; each check-in requires choosing the person |
| Member belongs to two churches | One account, separate tenant profiles and separate consents |
| Consent withdrawn | Geofences removed immediately; past records remain per retention policy |
| New SIM or phone | Re-verify by OTP; old device is revoked |
| Permission revoked in OS settings | App detects it and shows a gentle prompt with the fallback options |

