## 7. Design Brief

### 7.1 Brand and tone

Warm, welcoming and trustworthy; reverent without being stiff, modern without being corporate. The visual reference is the soft-card dashboard template (attached image): a light canvas, large rounded white cards, a slim purple side tab with icons, an indigo accent and a friendly greeting header. The base product stays denominationally neutral, and each church can add its own logo and accent colour.

### 7.2 Design principles

1. **Calm and glanceable.** The home screen answers one question: what is next, and am I checked in?
2. **Privacy you can see.** Consent and data controls are visible, plain language and never hidden in settings.
3. **Every age.** Large text, big touch targets and simple words, so a 70-year-old member and a 17-year-old volunteer both succeed.
4. **Fast on weak networks.** Light screens, skeleton loaders and clear offline states.
5. **Forgiving.** Every automatic action can be corrected in one tap.

### 7.3 Visual direction

| Element | Direction |
|---|---|
| Layout | Light canvas with white rounded cards (16 to 24 px radius), a slim icon sidebar, a greeting header and a card grid; cards can be shown or hidden per role |
| Palette | Indigo #6D5CF2 primary (sidebar, active states, main buttons), deep navy #1D1B3A for headings and the dark button, soft lilac #EFEDFF for tints, mint #7AD3B6 for success, coral #EF5A6F for high priority, warm gold #D9A441 used sparingly. Dark mode tokens are in the dashboard prototype |
| Typography | Plus Jakarta Sans (or Inter); greeting 28 to 44 px bold, card titles 17 px, body at least 14 px |
| Cards | White, soft shadow, 20 px padding, a header row with the title and a small action such as Edit or Clear |
| Components | Pill tags (High, Care call), progress bars and rings, avatar stacks, Light and Dark toggle, dashed Add new tiles, a floating hover card for the next event |
| Illustrations | Original line-and-fill illustrations in the same style, used in empty states and onboarding |
| Touch targets | 48 dp minimum on mobile |
| Modes | Light and dark |
| Accessibility | WCAG 2.2 AA contrast, never colour alone for status |

### 7.4 Key screen concepts

