## 8. Database Schema

PostgreSQL 16 with PostGIS. Every tenant-owned table has tenant_id and a row-level security policy. Shown below is the core schema; supporting lookup tables are omitted.

### 8.1 Entity overview

| Area | Tables |
|---|---|
| Tenancy | tenants, campuses, geofences, beacons |
| People | households, persons, groups, group_members |
| Access | users, user_roles, devices, consents |
| Services | services, service_instances |
| Attendance | attendance_signals, attendance_records, checkin_tokens |
| Care | followup_tasks, pastoral_notes |
| Communication | message_templates, messages, message_deliveries |
| Giving | funds, donations |
| Governance | audit_log |

### 8.2 Core DDL

```sql
create extension if not exists pgcrypto;
create extension if not exists postgis;
create extension if not exists citext;

create table tenants (
  id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),
